  "pinNotes": {
    "8": [
      "Drives the on-board WS2812 RGB LED. Also a strapping pin."
    ],
    "9": [
      "Wired to the BOOT button. Held LOW at reset it enters the download mode."
    ],
    "15": [
      "Blue user LED. Also a strapping pin, so avoid holding it at boot."
    ]
  },
  "notes": [
    "ESP32-C6 SuperMini (MakerGO): 22.5 x 18 mm, bare ESP32-C6FH4 with a PCB trace antenna, USB-C, on-board LiPo charger. 20 GPIOs on two 10-pin castellated rows at 2.54 mm.",
    "Same outline as the ESP32-C3 SuperMini but a completely different GPIO map - do not reuse a C3 SuperMini pinout here.",
    "GPIO15 drives the blue user LED; GPIO8 drives the WS2812 RGB LED.",
    "GPIO12/13 (USB D-/D+) and GPIO21/22/23 sit on unpopulated inner pads, not on the headers."
  ],
